proposed.construction:
For fixed \(H\), \(K\), and \(\varepsilon\in(0,1)\), \(\operatorname{QIR}_{H,K,\varepsilon}(\mathsf P,\mathfrak I)\) means the following single quantitative-inference regularity predicate for a triangular law--estimator sequence.  Every law is in \(\mathfrak M_H\); \(H\) and \(K\) do not vary with \(n\); \(g_a=\mathsf P(R=a)\ge\varepsilon\) and \(\mathsf P(S_k^a=1)\ge\varepsilon\) for both arms; and every supported factual at-risk continuation probability \(g_\ell^a(\mathcal H_{\ell-1}^a)\) is at least \(\varepsilon\).  The number of cross-fitting folds is fixed and their proportions are bounded away from zero.  Every training-fold estimate \(\widehat Q_{\ell,F}^a\) is clipped to \([0,1]\), every \(\widehat g_\ell^a\) is clipped to \([\varepsilon/2,1]\), and, uniformly over the sequence and over the finite collection \(F\in\{F_{bt}^1,F_w^0,F_S^0\}\), all these fits are \(L^2(\mathsf P)\)-consistent.  Finally,
\[
 \sum_{a,F}\sum_{\ell=1}^{K}
 \lVert\widehat Q_{\ell-1,F}^a-Q_{\ell-1,F}^a\rVert_2
 \left(\sum_{j=1}^{\ell}
 \lVert\widehat g_j^a-g_j^a\rVert_2\right)
 =o_{\mathsf P}(n^{-1/2})                                \tag{1}
\]
uniformly over the sequence.  Thus the predicate states quantitative assignment, survival, and factual censoring overlap, cross-fitting and clipping, uniform nuisance consistency, and the explicit longitudinal regression--censoring product-rate condition; it makes no restriction on unsupported switched-arm censoring.
